# Testing and code quality

The only verified package script for validation is `npm run build`. There is no lint script and no test runner. Do not add Jest, Playwright, ESLint, or another dependency in order to check a change.

- Run `npm run build` before opening a pull request when Node.js and dependencies are available locally.
- Do not treat `npm run dev` or `npm run start` as proof a change is correct.
- For UI changes, exercise the touched flow: Washington search filters, map ZIP lookup, owner sign-in and claims, and admin review. A screenshot of the first paint is not enough.
- TypeScript is strict in `tsconfig.json`. Do not silence a new error with `any` or a blanket `@ts-expect-error`.
- Do not commit `.env`, `node_modules`, or `.next`.

```text
# Existing validation command
npm run build
```

If Node.js or a lockfile is unavailable, say so in the pull request. Do not invent a passing check.
